Thanks, Pierre.

Sumti that are attached to a selbri in a place that is undefined in
jbovlaste, get a "context dependend" meaning. It would be very stretchy to
interpret the tunlo2 differently from "what is being swallowed". That said,
I think that tunlo2 should have been defined this way since the beginning :)

About lo/le, I have the habit of switching to {le} when I talk about a
specific thing that might have been introduced with {lo}.
After having said {lo labno noi ....} any time I write {le labno} I mean
*that* wolf. If I wrote {lo labno} I might mean another wolf.
Actually I do expect the listener to understand which one I mean, of course
I'm not guaranteed that he/she will but, if I'm careful, I hope I can be
understood. Otherwise it would rather useless to me.



